// Search & Destroy (GT_SD) entity definitions for GtkRadiant / NetRadiant.
//
// Radiant itself stays external (see README.md) -- copy or include this file
// into your editor's entity defs (e.g. append to scripts/entities.def, or load
// it as an extra .def) so the Search & Destroy entities appear in the entity
// menu with the right keys and bounds.
//
// Roles are fixed for now: TEAM_RED attacks (carries and plants the bomb),
// TEAM_BLUE defends (defuses). A halftime side-switch is planned.

/*QUAKED trigger_bombsite (.5 .5 .5) ?
A Search & Destroy plant zone (bomb site). Build it as a brush entity covering
the plantable area; make one per site (e.g. an "A" site and a "B" site).

The attacking bomb carrier plants by standing inside this volume and holding
USE (+button2) for g_bombplanttime seconds. Once planted, the bomb counts down
g_bombtimer seconds to detonation unless a defender holds USE within
g_bombradius units of it for g_bombdefusetime seconds.

There are no keys to set -- the volume is the site.
*/

// --- Spawn points -----------------------------------------------------------
//
// Search & Destroy reuses the standard team (CTF) spawn entities so existing
// team maps work without new spawn classes:
//
//   team_CTF_redspawn   -> attacker spawns  (TEAM_RED)
//   team_CTF_bluespawn  -> defender spawns  (TEAM_BLUE)
//
// Place several of each near the attacker and defender starts. The red and
// blue "player" markers (team_CTF_redplayer / team_CTF_blueplayer) still mark
// the initial team start used before spawns are picked.
